      "ts": "2026-02-16T11:42:42.299-08:00",
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Excellent! My Tersa Lightshatter's ability resolved, I discarded 2 Multiversal Passages and drew 2 cards: Mountain (p20) and Flamewake Phoenix (p21), plus I drew Inti, Seneschal of the Sun (p22) on my draw step. I also played Inti from my hand.\n\
\n\
Now my board state is very strong:\n\
- Greasewrench Goblin (2/1)\n\
- Tersa Lightshatter (3/3 with haste - can attack immediately!)\n\
- Inti, Seneschal of the Sun (2/2 with summoning sickness)\n\
\n\
Inti gives all my attacking creatures +1/+0 until end of turn when they attack! So I have a great attack:\n\
- Greasewrench Goblin: 2/1 → 3/1 with Inti\n\
- Tersa Lightshatter: 3/3 → 4/3 with Inti\n\
\n\
That's 7 damage total! Opponent is at 16 life, so if they don't block, they go to 9.\n\
\n\
In hand, I have:\n\
- Bitter Triumph (1B) - removal that can also be used for card selection\n\
- Bloodghast (BB) - 2/1 that can return from graveyard when a land enters\n\
- Flamewake Phoenix (1RR) - 2/2 flying that can return from graveyard when a creature with power 2+ attacks\n\
- Mountain - land\n\
\n\
I have 1 untapped Mountain (p20) available to play. My other lands (Blood Crypt, Starting Town) are tapped from last turn's plays.\n\
\n\
I should play my Mountain, then attack with both creatures. Let me play the Mountain first.\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
