    {
      "ts": "2026-02-16T11:43:19.407-08:00",
      "player": "DSV3 Libby",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Great! Inti's triggered ability is on the stack: \"Whenever you attack, you may discard a card. When you do, put a +1/+1 counter on target attacking creature. It gains trample until end of turn.\" This is a \"may\" ability, so I can choose to use it or not.\n\
\n\
I should consider discarding a card to put a +1/+1 counter on one of my attackers. Looking at my hand:\n\
- Bitter Triumph (1B) - removal, could be useful\n\
- Bloodghast (BB) - can come back from graveyard if I have a land enter, but I already played my land for turn\n\
- Flamewake Phoenix (1RR) - can come back from graveyard if I have a creature with power 2+ attack\n\
\n\
Actually, Bloodghast can return from my graveyard when a land enters the battlefield under my control. Since I already played my land for turn, it won't come back this turn. But I could discard Bloodghast, then it will be in my graveyard ready to come back if I draw a land next turn.\n\
\n\
Flamewake Phoenix can return from my graveyard if I have a creature with power 2 or greater attack. I have Tersa Lightshatter (3/3) and Greasewrench Goblin (2/1) attacking, so Flamewake could come back next combat if I discard it now. However, I don't have RR to cast it from my hand if I need it this turn, and discarding it to Inti's ability puts it in my graveyard where I can return it for free when a creature with power 2+ attacks.\n\
\n\
Actually wait, reading Inti's ability more carefully: \"Whenever you attack, you may discard a card. When you do, put a +1/+1 counter on target attacking creature. It gains trample until end of turn.\" It has two parts:\n\
1. \"you may discard a card\" - this is optional\n\
2. \"When you do\" (when you discard a card), put a +1/+1 counter...\n\
\n\
So I can choose to discard a card, and if I do, I get to put a +1/+1 counter on an attacking creature. The discard is part of the cost.\n\
\n\
I have 3 cards in hand. I could discard Bloodghast since I can't cast it this turn anyway (BB cost, I have 2 Mountains untapped but no Black sources untapped). Or I could discard Bitter Triumph if I think I won't need removal this turn. Or Flamewake Phoenix.\n\
\n\
Actually, looking at my board: I have 2 attackers, Greasewrench Goblin (2/1) and Tersa Lightshatter (3/3). With Inti's static ability, they get +1/+0 when attacking, so they're currently 3/1 and 4/3. If I put a +1/+1 counter on Greasewrench Goblin, it becomes a 4/2 with trample (after Inti's +1/+0). That's nice.\n\
\n\
But if I put the counter on Tersa Lightshatter, it becomes a 5/4 with trample. That's even better. However, the opponent has no blockers, so trample doesn't matter. The +1/+1 counter is permanent though, so I should put it on whichever creature I think will be more valuable long-term.\n\
\n\
Greasewrench Goblin has the exhaust ability (2R: discard up to two cards, then draw that many cards and put a +1/+1 counter on Greasewrench Goblin). So it can grow itself over time. Tersa Lightshatter doesn't have any growth ability.\n\
\n\
I think I should discard Bloodghast and put the counter on Tersa Lightshatter to make it a 4/4 (or 5/4 with Inti's bonus). Bloodghast is fine in the graveyard - it can come back when a land enters.\n\
\n\
Let me choose to use the ability:\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
